# EPUB corpus manifest
#
# Every line: <local-name> <sha256> <bytes> <url>
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# The files themselves are NOT committed -- ~40 MiB of binaries, and Project
# Gutenberg regenerates its artifacts, so a committed copy would silently drift
# from what the sources actually serve. The digest is the anchor: fetch_corpus.py
# refuses any download whose SHA-256 does not match, so a regenerated upstream
# artifact fails loudly instead of quietly changing ADR-013's numbers.
#
# Downloaded 2026-08-30. Three groups, chosen to separate "the packer's habits"
# from "the ceiling is wrong":
#   gutenberg-*   Project Gutenberg EPUB 2 (.epub.noimages)  -- coarse packing
#   gutenberg3-*  Project Gutenberg EPUB 3 (.epub3.images)   -- same texts, EPUB 3 packer
#   se-*          Standard Ebooks                            -- one chapter per file
#
# All titles are public domain in the United States. Gutenberg content carries the
# Project Gutenberg License; Standard Ebooks releases to the public domain via CC0.
# The corpus is used for measurement only -- no text is redistributed here, and no
# fixture from it ships in the app.

